<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dong Jieyuan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">late 12th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dong Jieyuan was a writer of the Jin dynasty, active in the late twelfth century, whose real name is unknown; Jieyuan was an honorific title for a top examination candidate. He wrote a long version of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romance-of-the-western-chamber">Romance of the Western Chamber</a> in the zhugongdiao form, a sung narrative mixing verse in many musical modes with prose. It is the only complete work of that genre to survive and was the main source of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wang-shifu">Wang Shifu</a>'s later drama.</p></div>
